From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 77450danik <ddziuba1@stu.vistula.edu.pl>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 19:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] mountmgr.sys: Every disk answers with its number, size and what it read and wrote.

The Task Manager showed one disk, C:, with the sum of all of them. Every
drive now finds the physical disk under its folder (down through the live
mode's device-mapper snapshot and loop devices) and answers as Windows'
disk drivers do:

- IOCTL_DISK_PERFORMANCE with the disk's bytes, requests, times and idle
  time from /sys/block/<disk>/stat (DISK_PERFORMANCE was not declared);
- IOCTL_STORAGE_GET_DEVICE_NUMBER with one number for all volumes of a disk,
  the disk Windows is on being 0, NVMe disks next, then the others by name;
- IOCTL_DISK_GET_DRIVE_GEOMETRY_EX with the disk's real size;
- StorageDeviceProperty with its model and NVMe bus, and
  StorageDeviceSeekPenaltyProperty saying whether it is a hard disk.
---
